  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q58-group-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following expressions.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p31-q58-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{x^2+2x+1}{4x-1}\\times\\frac{16x^2-1}{x^2-1}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{(x+1)(4x+1)}{x-1}$, $x\\ne\\frac14,1,-1$.\n\nFactorise the perfect square and differences of squares, then cancel common factors.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^2+2x+1}{4x-1}\\times\\frac{16x^2-1}{x^2-1}&=\\frac{(x+1)^2}{4x-1}\\times\\frac{(4x-1)(4x+1)}{(x-1)(x+1)}\\\\\\frac{x^2+2x+1}{4x-1}\\times\\frac{16x^2-1}{x^2-1}&=\\frac{(x+1)(4x+1)}{x-1}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominators require $x\\ne\\frac14,1,-1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q59-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{x^2-9x+20}{x^2-5x+4}\\times\\frac{x^2-3x+2}{x^2-5x+6}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{x-5}{x-3}$, $x\\ne1,2,3,4$.\n\nFactorise all four quadratics before cancelling.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^2-9x+20}{x^2-5x+4}\\times\\frac{x^2-3x+2}{x^2-5x+6}&=\\frac{(x-5)(x-4)}{(x-1)(x-4)}\\times\\frac{(x-1)(x-2)}{(x-2)(x-3)}\\\\\\frac{x^2-9x+20}{x^2-5x+4}\\times\\frac{x^2-3x+2}{x^2-5x+6}&=\\frac{x-5}{x-3}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominators require $x\\ne1,2,3,4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q60-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{x^2-2x}{x^2+x-6}\\times\\frac{x^2-2x-15}{x^3-25x}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac1{x+5}$, $x\\ne-5,-3,0,2,5$.\n\nExtract common factors and factorise fully before cancelling.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^2-2x}{x^2+x-6}\\times\\frac{x^2-2x-15}{x^3-25x}&=\\frac{x(x-2)}{(x+3)(x-2)}\\times\\frac{(x-5)(x+3)}{x(x-5)(x+5)}\\\\\\frac{x^2-2x}{x^2+x-6}\\times\\frac{x^2-2x-15}{x^3-25x}&=\\frac1{x+5}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominators require $x\\ne-5,-3,0,2,5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q61-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac4{x^2+3x+2}+\\frac3{x+1}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{3x+10}{(x+1)(x+2)}$, $x\\ne-1,-2$.\n\nFactorise the quadratic denominator and use a common denominator.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac4{x^2+3x+2}+\\frac3{x+1}&=\\frac4{(x+1)(x+2)}+\\frac{3(x+2)}{(x+1)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac4{x^2+3x+2}+\\frac3{x+1}&=\\frac{4+3x+6}{(x+1)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac4{x^2+3x+2}+\\frac3{x+1}&=\\frac{3x+10}{(x+1)(x+2)}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominators require $x\\ne-1,-2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q62-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac1{x^2-25}+\\frac1{x^2+6x+5}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{2(x-2)}{(x-5)(x+1)(x+5)}$, $x\\ne-5,-1,5$.\n\nFactorise both denominators, then combine over their common denominator.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{x^2-25}+\\frac1{x^2+6x+5}&=\\frac1{(x-5)(x+5)}+\\frac1{(x+1)(x+5)}\\\\\\frac1{x^2-25}+\\frac1{x^2+6x+5}&=\\frac{(x+1)+(x-5)}{(x-5)(x+1)(x+5)}\\\\\\frac1{x^2-25}+\\frac1{x^2+6x+5}&=\\frac{2(x-2)}{(x-5)(x+1)(x+5)}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominators require $x\\ne-5,-1,5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q63-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{3x^2+1}{x^2-4x-12}-\\frac1{x-6}-\\frac1{x+2}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{3x^2-2x+5}{(x-6)(x+2)}$, $x\\ne6,-2$.\n\nUse a common denominator and subtract each entire numerator.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3x^2+1}{x^2-4x-12}-\\frac1{x-6}-\\frac1{x+2}&=\\frac{3x^2+1}{(x-6)(x+2)}-\\frac{x+2}{(x-6)(x+2)}-\\frac{x-6}{(x-6)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac{3x^2+1}{x^2-4x-12}-\\frac1{x-6}-\\frac1{x+2}&=\\frac{3x^2+1-(x+2)-(x-6)}{(x-6)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac{3x^2+1}{x^2-4x-12}-\\frac1{x-6}-\\frac1{x+2}&=\\frac{3x^2-2x+5}{(x-6)(x+2)}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominators require $x\\ne6,-2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q64-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-4xy-12y^2}-\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-12xy+36y^2}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\dfrac{8y}{(x+2y)(x-6y)}$, $x\\ne6y,-2y$.\n\nFactorise and cancel within each fraction, then subtract using a common denominator.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-4xy-12y^2}-\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-12xy+36y^2}&=\\frac{x-6y}{(x-6y)(x+2y)}-\\frac{x-6y}{(x-6y)^2}\\\\\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-4xy-12y^2}-\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-12xy+36y^2}&=\\frac1{x+2y}-\\frac1{x-6y}\\\\\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-4xy-12y^2}-\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-12xy+36y^2}&=\\frac{(x-6y)-(x+2y)}{(x+2y)(x-6y)}\\\\\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-4xy-12y^2}-\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-12xy+36y^2}&=-\\frac{8y}{(x+2y)(x-6y)}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominators require $x\\ne6y$ and $x\\ne-2y$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 90
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q65-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{\\dfrac{3}{x^2-x-6}}{\\dfrac{2}{x+2}+\\dfrac{1}{x-3}}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{3}{3x-4}$, where $x\\ne-2,3,\\dfrac43$.",
          "worked": "Factor the quadratic denominator and combine the fractions in the divisor.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\dfrac{\\dfrac{3}{x^2-x-6}}{\\dfrac{2}{x+2}+\\dfrac{1}{x-3}}&=\\dfrac{3}{(x-3)(x+2)}\\div\\dfrac{2(x-3)+(x+2)}{(x+2)(x-3)}\\\\\\dfrac{\\dfrac{3}{x^2-x-6}}{\\dfrac{2}{x+2}+\\dfrac{1}{x-3}}&=\\dfrac{3}{(x-3)(x+2)}\\times\\dfrac{(x+2)(x-3)}{3x-4}\\\\\\dfrac{\\dfrac{3}{x^2-x-6}}{\\dfrac{2}{x+2}+\\dfrac{1}{x-3}}&=\\dfrac{3}{3x-4}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominators require $x\\ne-2,3$. The divisor must also be nonzero, so $x\\ne\\dfrac43$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 100
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q66-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{\\dfrac1{x-2}+\\dfrac1{x-5}}{\\dfrac1{x-1}+\\dfrac1{x-6}}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{(x-1)(x-6)}{(x-2)(x-5)}$, where $x\\ne1,2,5,6,\\dfrac72$.",
          "worked": "Combine each pair of fractions before dividing.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\dfrac{\\dfrac1{x-2}+\\dfrac1{x-5}}{\\dfrac1{x-1}+\\dfrac1{x-6}}&=\\dfrac{2x-7}{(x-2)(x-5)}\\div\\dfrac{2x-7}{(x-1)(x-6)}\\\\\\dfrac{\\dfrac1{x-2}+\\dfrac1{x-5}}{\\dfrac1{x-1}+\\dfrac1{x-6}}&=\\dfrac{2x-7}{(x-2)(x-5)}\\times\\dfrac{(x-1)(x-6)}{2x-7}\\\\\\dfrac{\\dfrac1{x-2}+\\dfrac1{x-5}}{\\dfrac1{x-1}+\\dfrac1{x-6}}&=\\dfrac{(x-1)(x-6)}{(x-2)(x-5)}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominators require $x\\ne1,2,5,6$. The divisor must be nonzero, so $x\\ne\\dfrac72$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 104
      }
    ]
  },
